_pacman_updater_message() {
    cat <<'EOF'

pacman-updater administrator setup:

  This package does not create users, modify sudoers, or enable systemd units.
  If the optional AUR update stage is enabled, configure aur_user and create
  that account separately.

  Do not grant aur_user unrestricted sudo access. Review the installed wrapper
  before adding any sudoers rule. If it is verified to constrain its arguments,
  a narrowly scoped rule may be appropriate:

    aur_user ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/lib/pacman-updater/pacman-updater-pacman-wrapper

  Never grant direct unrestricted access to pacman, makepkg, or yay because
  package build scripts can execute arbitrary commands.

  Both units are installed disabled. After reviewing the configuration and
  administrator-controlled privilege setup, enable the scheduled updater with:

    sudo systemctl enable --now pacman-updater.timer

  The timer will start pacman-updater.service on its schedule. To run one
  update immediately, use `sudo systemctl start pacman-updater.service`.

EOF
}

post_install() {
    _pacman_updater_message
}

post_upgrade() {
    _pacman_updater_message
}
